---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../../consts';

const contactEmail = 'simsanghyeon00@gmail.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${SITE_TITLE} Clips for Slack - Terms of Service`}
  description="Terms of Service for Half to Full Clips for Slack."
  langAlternate={null}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Half to Full Clips for Slack</p>
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: April 28, 2026</p>

    <p>
      These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of Half to Full Clips for
      Slack ("the app"). By installing or using the app, you agree to these Terms.
      If you install the app for a Slack workspace, you represent that you have
      permission to do so for that workspace.
    </p>

    <h2>Service description</h2>
    <p>
      The app sends notifications to a Slack channel when a new Clip is published
      on Half to Full. A Clip is a public post containing a short personal
      comment, an external source link, and optional quote or tags.
    </p>

    <h2>Slack permissions</h2>
    <p>
      The app requests Slack's <code>incoming-webhook</code> permission so it can
      post Clip notifications to the channel selected during installation. The
      app does not request permission to read Slack messages, files, user
      profiles, or conversation history.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You agree not to use the app to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Violate laws, regulations, Slack policies, or third-party rights.</li>
      <li>Attempt to access, extract, or misuse app secrets or webhook URLs.</li>
      <li>Interfere with the operation, security, or availability of the app.</li>
      <li>Use the app in a way that misrepresents its relationship with Slack or Half to Full.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Content and external links</h2>
    <p>
      Clip notifications may include links to public posts on Half to Full and to
      third-party articles. Third-party websites are controlled by their own
      operators and may have their own terms and privacy practices.
    </p>

    <h2>Fees</h2>
    <p>
      The app is currently provided free of charge. If this changes, the app's
      listing and related pages will be updated before paid use is required.
    </p>

    <h2>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>
      The app is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. We may update,
      suspend, or discontinue the app, or change these Terms, when needed for
      maintenance, security, legal, or product reasons.
    </p>

    <h2>Uninstalling and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      You may uninstall the app from Slack at any time. To request deletion of
      stored installation data, contact
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> with your Slack
      workspace name or workspace ID.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the app is provided
      without warranties of any kind. We are not liable for indirect, incidental,
      special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of the
      app.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For questions about these Terms, email
      <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .eyebrow,
  .updated {
    color: rgb(var(--gray));
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
